Objective:
Transform my draft recipe book into a polished, professional cookbook suitable for publication.

Instructions:
Use Kennys Recipes Book – AI Test.docx as the source document. Edit and format each recipe so it is clear, consistent, and easy for readers to follow.

For every recipe:
•	Correct grammar, spelling, and punctuation.
•	Standardize all measurements and units (e.g., tablespoon vs. Tbsp, cup, teaspoon) and ensure consistency throughout the book.
•	Improve clarity without changing the original intent or flavor of the recipes.

Required Recipe Structure:
Each recipe must be organized using the following sections, in this exact order:
1.	Title
2.	Servings
3.	Ingredients
4.	Preparation
5.	Cooking
6.	Homesteader’s Tip (practical, self-sufficient, or farm-inspired advice related to the recipe)

Formatting Requirements:
•	Use clean, professional cookbook formatting.
•	Ensure consistent tone and style across all recipes.
•	Create a Table of Contents
•	Use image Homestead.life-Cover-Image for the cover
•	Add a footer to each recipe page that reads: @HybridHomestead.life

Output Goal:
A cohesive, publication-ready recipe book that reflects a homestead-style approach and is accessible to everyday cooks.

Lock Fidelity Mode: preserve exact ingredients and amounts from the source. Only grammar, formatting, and section structure were applied. No substitutions. No inferred changes. No fixes.
